      "content": "\"think outside the box\" and \"meeting client expectations\" sounds like standard corporate speak, not the aggressive drive we need. To be honest, if he's just a methodical guy who likes structure, he might actually hinder our speed rather than help it. \n\nIf you look closely at his responses regarding conflict or rapid pivots, does he actually sound like someone who can make hard, split-second decisions under fire, or is he more of a \"process and consensus\" type? I don't want to waste the VP's time if he's going to be too slow for us.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
